{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"RevcontentSDK"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Theme integration"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coordinate the widget’s appearance with your app’s color scheme."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"RevcontentSDK bridges SwiftUI’s color scheme into the embedded widget via two channels:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"overrideUserInterfaceStyle"},{"text":", so any CSS using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)"},{"text":" resolves correctly.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revcontent:theme"},{"text":" JavaScript event dispatched to the widget on change, so widget code can react explicitly.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both fire whenever the resolved SwiftUI color scheme changes — at first load and on every subsequent toggle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Letting-the-widget-inherit-the-system-scheme","text":"Letting the widget inherit the system scheme","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, ","type":"text"},{"code":"RevcontentAdView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inherits the color scheme from the SwiftUI environment, which is driven by the user’s system setting. No extra code required:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["RevcontentAdView(widgetId: \"abc-123\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the user toggles dark mode in Settings, the widget receives a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revcontent:theme"},{"text":" event and its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"overrideUserInterfaceStyle"},{"text":" updates accordingly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Forcing-a-specific-scheme","text":"Forcing a specific scheme","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Override the color scheme with the dedicated modifier:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["RevcontentAdView(widgetId: \"abc-123\")","    .revcontentColorScheme(.dark)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is equivalent to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".environment(\\.colorScheme, .dark)"},{"type":"text","text":" but reads more clearly. Use it when you want the widget pinned to a specific appearance regardless of system setting — for example, inside an in-app reader that’s always dark."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also use SwiftUI’s built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".preferredColorScheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" higher up the view tree to set the scheme app-wide; the widget will follow."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-the-widget-should-do","text":"What the widget should do","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The widget’s CSS and JavaScript should respect both bridge channels:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"CSS","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { ... }"},{"type":"text","text":" for dark-mode styles. The SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"overrideUserInterfaceStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" ensures this resolves correctly inside the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"JavaScript"}]},{"type":"text","text":": optionally listen for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revcontent:theme"},{"type":"text","text":" events on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"document"},{"type":"text","text":" if the widget needs to react imperatively. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/JSEventContract","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the payload shape."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Articles","title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/ScrollContextPlacement","doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/UIKitAndObjectiveC","doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/JSEventContract"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/ThemeIntegration","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Related","title":"Related","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/SwiftUICore\/View\/revcontentColorScheme(_:)","doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/JSEventContract"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/revcontentsdk\/themeintegration"]},{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/revcontentsdk\/themeintegration"]}],"references":{"doc://com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK/documentation/RevcontentSDK/JSEventContract":{"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.revcontent.RevcontentSDK\/documentation\/RevcontentSDK\/JSEventContract","title":"JavaScript event contract","url":"\/documentation\/revcontentsdk\/jseventcontract","abstract":[{"text":"Events the SDK dispatches into the embedded 